A bracket path that doesn't exist is a glob pattern: `[ab].md` matches `a.md` and `b.md` as a character class, so the glob view leaves out `c.md`.
== args
input/[ab].md
== file input/a.md
---
description: File a.
---
# a
== file input/b.md
---
description: File b.
---
# b
== file input/c.md
---
description: File c.
---
# c
== stdout
glob view: input/[ab].md
input/a.md (4 lines): description: "File a."
input/b.md (4 lines): description: "File b."
== stderr
== exit 0
